## Multi-Agent Architecture

### Model serving strategy
- **Dev:** Ollama local — `AsyncClient()` from `ollama` package
- **Prod:** Together.ai — Hermes-3-Llama-3.1-8B at `$0.18/1M` tokens
- **One base model + N LoRA adapters** — never 5 separate model instances
- Adapter naming: `csr-hermes-deposit`, `csr-hermes-withdrawal`, etc.
- Temperature: always `0.1` for CSR responses — never above `0.3`

### Router
- GPT-4o-mini with structured output for MVP (cheap, fast, accurate)
- Pydantic `IntentResult` model with `response_format=IntentResult`
- Confidence < 0.7 → always route to `general` agent (safe fallback)
- Never route to `verification` agent on confidence < 0.85 (KYC is sensitive)

---

## Semantic Cache

- Upstash Vector index — initialized once at module level
- Similarity threshold: `SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD = 0.92` — constant, not magic number
- Embedding model: `nomic-embed-text` via Ollama, 768-dim
- Cache key: `sha256(f"{tenant_id}:{query}")` — always tenant-scoped
- TTL: `604800` (7 days) for quality_score ≥ 0.80, `86400` (24h) otherwise
- Cache write is async and non-blocking — fire and forget after response is sent

---

## Auditor (LLM Judge)

- Model: `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` — cheapest capable model
- Sample rate: `0.05` (5%) — constant at top of file
- **Always async** — never block the main inference path
- If Anthropic API errors: log and continue, never fail the user response
- Score threshold for flagging: composite < 0.6 OR hallucination_risk > 0.5
- Fire via `asyncio.create_task()` — not `await`

---

## Training Pipeline (pipeline/)

### Data quality thresholds
- Minimum quality score to include in training: `0.65`
- High-quality threshold (2× weight): `0.90`
- Minimum examples before training run: `200`
- Recommended before production fine-tune: `500`

### Replay buffer ratio
- 70% historical (best examples from previous runs)
- 30% new examples from current collection period
- **Never fine-tune on new data only** — catastrophic forgetting

